Has anyone ever seen ghost shutdowns ? I.e. the machine starts to shut down 
cleanly like you'd just issued a shutdown -h now, except you haven't ? :) 
And with no error message or log message to signal anything abnormal (like 
thermal overheat or battery critical). This is also with an AC connected 
laptop.. it happens once every few days.

Using 2.4.21+acpi, so it's not the latest ACPI, but I thought I'd might ask 
if it's an error seen before. It does not have to have anything to do with 
ACPI of course. I should run with ACPI debug enabled I guess and see if it 
says anything before the shutdowns.. 

